    sb: el: sync 2026.21.01 and 2026.23.01 release updates (#2736)
    
    Summary:
    ## Title
    
    This PR syncs the **Santa Barbara Electra** release updates from **2026.21.01** through **2026.23.01**.
    
    The changes mainly cover shell and display updates, EVB-specific behavior cleanup, bootstrap default and persistence handling, IO expander configuration updates, sensor naming and hook fixes, PLDM TID alignment, and minor SRAM/debug cleanup.
    
    ## Features
    
    * Add `voltage set <voltage-rail> <new-voltage>` shell command support
    
      * Restrict voltage setting to VR test mode
      * Validate target voltage against configured min/max range
      * Reject OSFP P3V3 voltage setting
    
    * Add MFIO16 bootstrap status shell command
    
      * Read MFIO16 bootstrap status from CPLD
      * Show HAMSA, NUWA0, and NUWA1 MFIO16 status
    
    * Use platform EID as PLDM TID
    
      * Add `plat_pldm_get_tid()`
      * Set PLDM TID to platform EID
    
    * Update EVB-only shell behavior for OSFP P3V3
    
      * Restrict `voltage_range` OSFP P3V3 query to EVB boards
      * Skip OSFP rail handling in `vr_status` on non-EVB platforms
    
    * Update UBC power sensor post-read hook
    
      * Change `SENSOR_NUM_UBC1_P12V_PWR_W` from `post_common_sensor_read` to `post_ubc_read`
      * Change `SENSOR_NUM_UBC2_P12V_PWR_W` from `post_common_sensor_read` to `post_ubc_read`
    
    * Update bootstrap and IO expander behavior
    
      * Re-enable `pca6416a`, `tca6424a`, and `tcal6408r` initialization in `ioexp_init()`
      * Update `tca6424a` and `tcal6408r` init configuration
      * Modify bootstrap default values for `NUWA0_CHIP_STRAP_0`, `NUWA0_CHIP_STRAP_1`, `NUWA1_CHIP_STRAP_0`, and `NUWA1_CHIP_STRAP_1`
      * Fix bootstrap sync logic to preserve input bits
      * Add bootstrap permanent setting clear flow in `perm_config_clear`
    
    * Update display and naming
    
      * Replace `RB` with `EL` in display output
      * Replace `MEDHA` with `NUWA` in display output
      * Replace `IRIS` with `ARKE` in display output
      * Fix duplicated `ASIC` in sensor name
    
    * Miscellaneous cleanup
    
      * Add unit description and example to `sensor_threshold set` help
      * Update `LEAK_DETECT_REG` compare mask from `0xFF` to `0xDF`
      * Remove unused debug logs to reduce SRAM usage
    
    ## Included releases
    
    * 2026.21.01
    * 2026.23.01
    
