    common: fix NetFn comparison for OEM POST Start/End commands (#2693)
    
    Summary:
    Description
    The KCS input buffer (ibuf[0]) contains the Network Function (NetFn)
    shifted left by 2 bits to accommodate the LUN. The previous check
    compared the raw NETFN_OEM_REQ (0x30) against the shifted value (0xC0),
    causing the POST Start/End response logic to be skipped.
    
    This commit applies the left shift (<< 2) to NETFN_OEM_REQ during
    comparison, ensuring the KCS driver correctly identifies these OEM
    commands and returns the success completion code to the host.
    
    Motivation
    On the yv4-sd platform, BIOS was observed to repeatedly send POST Start
