    gc2: es: Fix false MP5998/TPS25990 UV fault/warning triggered during VIN startup (#2691)
    
    [Issue Description]
    - Related to GC20T5T7-154
    - MP5998 STATUS_WORD[79h] and STATUS_BYTE[78h] indicate VIN_UV_FAULT
      during startup; TPS25990 UV FLT and Warning registers get set during
      VIN ramp up after every AC power restore
    - False fault status bits remain set after startup completes, causing
      incorrect fault reporting in system health monitoring
    
    [Root Cause]
    - During VIN ramp up after AC power restore, both MP5998 and TPS25990
      inherently assert UV fault/warning bits in their status registers
    - These false fault bits are not self-clearing, so they persist and
      pollute the HSC fault status after the device has fully started up
    
    [Solution]
    - Add plat_sensor_clear_vr_fault() to issue PMBUS CLEAR_FAULTS command
      (command code 0x03) to the target HSC device via I2C as a workaround
      per power team's suggestion
    - Invoke the function during pal_get_extend_sensor_config() when
      HSC_MODULE_MP5990 is detected and AC loss is indicated by is_ac_lost(),
      ensuring fault bits are cleared once on every AC power restore
    
    [Test Log]
    - Verify UV fault/warning bits are cleared after AC power restore
    - Confirm HSC status registers show no false fault after power up
