    Summary:
    # [Task Description]
    - Related to GC20T5T7-92
    - Support SMI interrupt monitoring on BIC
    - If GPIO "IRQ_SMI_ACTIVE_BMC_N" remains low for 90 seconds, BIC will report an SMI-related event to BMC
    
    # [Motivation]
    - GPIO "IRQ_SMI_ACTIVE_BMC_N" is asserted low when the system enters SMI/SMM
    - If BIOS or firmware hangs in SMM, this GPIO may remain low indefinitely
    - Without monitoring, the failure cannot be recorded once the system becomes unresponsive
    - This mechanism allows BMC to log an error event for debugging
    
    # [Design]
    - Add SMI GPIO interrupt handler on BIC
    - Monitor IRQ_SMI_ACTIVE_BMC_N via edge-triggered interrupt
    - Start a 90-second timer when SMI is asserted
    - If GPIO remains low after 90 seconds, BIC reports SMI event to BMC
    - When GPIO is released, BIC reports deassertion event
    
    # [Test Log]
