    # [Task Description]
    - Related to GC20T5T7-58
    - During DC power cycle, the BMC may record unexpected assert/deassert SEL events related to MB_VR sensors. These events occur while the system is transitioning between power states and the VR sensors are not yet in a valid operating condition.
    - This change improves VR sensor accessibility handling and prevents false alarm SEL entries during DC power transitions.
    
    # [Root Cause]
    - A race condition exists between sensor polling and DC power status updates. In some cases, the BIC reads VR sensor data before the DC_STATUS flag is updated to OFF, even though the actual DC power GPIO (PWRGD_SYS_PWROK) has already transitioned to low. This mismatch causes invalid VR readings to be interpreted as real sensor events, resulting in false SEL logs.
    
    # [Solution]
    - Override the common vr_access() function with a platform-specific implementation.
    - The GC2-ES platform vr_access() directly checks the real DC power GPIO (PWRGD_SYS_PWROK) and only allows VR sensor access when DC power is confirmed to be on. This ensures VR sensors are not polled during DC-off or transient power states.
    
    # [Test Log]
    - Verify no false assert/deassert SEL entries are generated for MB_VR sensors during DC cycle.
