    fby4: wf: Check DIMM present status before reading temperature (#2604)
    
    Summary:
    - Related to YV4T1M-2159
    - Refer to SD BIC implementation to add a pre_hook function that checks DIMM present status before reading DIMM temperature
    - Implement a CCI Mailbox command to retrieve DIMM slot information, including present status, and store it in cache during platform init
    - Added two additional fixes related to initialization timing and DIMM temperature polling logic
    
    # Motivation:
    - Prevent BMC from reading invalid temperature data when DIMM is not installed
    - Ensure the fan fail-safe mode can be properly triggered when DIMM is not present
    
    # Design:
    - Use CCI Mailbox command to get DIMM slot info and present status
    - Store DIMM presence data in cache at platform initialization
    - Retrieve DIMM presence from cache before reading DIMM temperature
    - Mark the sensor as unavailable if DIMM is not present
    - Fix 1:
    Found that when certain DIMMs are not installed, PG_CARD_OK may assert later than expected, causing system initialization to be skipped. Added retry and timeout mechanisms to ensure initialization
    - Fix 2:
    Previously only DIMM_A performed real temperature reads and updated the cache, while all other DIMMs read from cache. This caused all DIMMs to fail when DIMM_A was absent. Updated the mechanism to select an existing DIMM as the Master DIMM during initialization so the Master DIMM handles actual temperature reads and cache updates
    
