    fby35: gl: Support E1S card type (#1342)
    
    Summary:
    # Description:
        The method that identifies the 1OU card type:
            1. E1S’s:
                - In CPLD register 05:
                    - BIT2 is low
                    - BIT0,1,4 are high.
                - ADC6(Extend card type) is lower than 0.3V
            2. Other 1OU board:
                - In CPLD register 05:
                    - BIT0,1,2 and 4 are low.
            3. No 1OU board
                - In CPLD register 05:
                    - BIT0,1,2 and 4 are high
    
    # Motivation:
        Support E1S card type in GreatLakes platform.
    
    Pull Request resolved: https://github.com/facebook/OpenBIC/pull/1342
    
    Test Plan:
    No board:
            uart:~$ i2c read I2C_0 0x21 0x05 1      //Get CPLD register 05h
            00000000: 1f    // BIT 0,1,2,4 are high
            uart:~$ i2c read I2C_0 0x21 0x09    // 1OU board Detection
            00000000: 00    // No 1OU board
            root@bmc-oob:~# bic-util slot3 0xe0 0xa1 0x15 0xa0 0x00 00  //Get 1OU card type
            15 A0 00 00 FEs     //No 1OU board
    
        E1S board:
            uart:~$ i2c read I2C_0 0x21 0x05 1
            00000000: 1b    // BIT 2 is low and BIT 0,1,4 are high
            uart:~$ i2c read I2C_0 0x21 0x09 1
            00000000: 0a    // E1S board
            root@bmc-oob:~# bic-util slot3 0xe0 0xa1 0x15 0xa0 0x00 00
            15 A0 00 00 0A  // E1S board
    
        Rainbow falls:
            uart:~$ i2c read I2C_0 0x21 0x05 1
            00000000: 08 // BIT 0,1,2,4 are low
            uart:~$ i2c read I2C_0 0x21 0x09 1
            00000000: 02    // Rainbow falls
            root@bmc-oob:~# bic-util slot3 0xe0 0xa1 0x15 0xa0 0x00 00
            15 A0 00 00 02 // Rainbow falls
    
