    Lora/artemis/meb support card present command (#828)
    
    Summary:
    Artemis: mc: Support ipmi OEM command to get pcie card status
    
    - Support IPMI OEM command to get pcie card status. (netfn: 0x38, cmd: 0x76)
    - Refactor ACB get ASIC card status IPMI OEM command. (netfn: 0x38, cmd: 0x76)
    - Improve find_FRU_ID function to return error code if BIC can't find fru_id in fru config table.
    - Modify ACB/MEB fru id to match the fru id defined in BMC.
    
    Note:
    - MEB IPMI command format
      - Request
        Byte 1:3 – MFG ID – 00A015h, LS byte first
        Byte 4 – FRU id (range: 30~43)
               – FRU id is mapped to JCN 1~14 card
        Byte 5 – PCIE device id (range: 0~2)
               – Device id 0: CXL or NIC or E1.S
               – Device id 1: E1.S 0
               – Device id 2: E1.S 1
      - Response
        Byte 1 – Completion Code
        Byte 2:4 – MFG ID – 00A015h, LS byte first
        Byte 5 – PCIE card/device presence status (0: not present, 1: present)
        Byte 6 – PCIE card type (Return unknown card if device not present)
                 – 0x00: E1S card
                 – 0x01: E1S_0 card
                 – 0x02: E1S_1 card
                 – 0x03: E1S_0 and E1S_1 card
                 – 0x04: NIC card
                 – 0x05: CXL card
                 – 0xFF: Unknown card
    
    - ACB IPMI command format
      - Request
        Byte 1:3 – MFG ID – 00A015h, LS byte first
        Byte 4 – FRU id (range: 13, 18~29)
               – FRU id is mapped to ASIC card 1~12
        Byte 5 – PCIE device id (range: 0~2)
               – Device id 0: FIO/ASIC card presence status
               – Device id 1: ASIC device 1 presence status
               – Device id 2: ASIC device 2 presence status
      - Response
        Byte 1 – Completion Code
        Byte 2:4 – MFG ID – 00A015h, LS byte first
        Byte 5 – FIO/ASIC card/device presence status (0x00: not present, 0x01: present, 0xFF: unknown status)
        Byte 6 – Reserve (Default value is 0)
    
