    fby3.5: rf: Support VR alert event recording. (#605)
    
    Summary:
    - Summury
    
      Implement the VR abnormal event recording mechanism.
    
      Once BIC detects a VR abnormal event by the specified alert GPIO, BIC will send two SELs to BMC. The event data[0] of these two SELs indicate the same probelm device but different page numbers. The remaining two event data are the respective VR status.
    
      Specified VR numbers are reserved to identify the problem device:
    
        3: 1OU_VR_P0V9/P0V8_ASICA , i2c address(7/8 bit): 64h/C8h
        4: 1OU_VR_VDDQAB/D0V8     , i2c address(7/8 bit): 58h/B0h
        5: 1OU_VR_VDDQCD          , i2c address(7/8 bit): 5Ah/B4h
    
    - Test Trigger the P0V8_ASICD VOUT fault event, and then the BMC will receive two SELs:
    
      ```
