    Fixed NVMe reading function (#84)
    
    Summary:
    - Added return value check, if temperature data is 0x80 or 0x81 means SSD temperature reading is in abnormal status and BIC should do error handling instead of keeping data as SSD temperature.
    
    Design:
    - According to NVME specification , getting 0x80 from SSD0 means no temperature data or the temperature data is not update over 5 seconds.
    - Retry three rounds to check if there is no temperature data keeping in SSD or not updating temperature data over 5 seconds. If error status keep more than 3 rounds continuously, BIC would set SSD status to abnormal and return SSD temperature NA to BMC.
    
    Pull Request resolved: https://github.com/facebook/OpenBIC/pull/84
    
    Test Plan:
    - Build code: Pass
    - Test 600 times DC cycle: Pass
    
